C. Issues Identified

Issue 1 — RLS Infinite Recursion Breaks applications & application_applicants Queries
Feature/Page Affected: /tenant/portal.html, /admin/applications.html, /admin/leases.html, /admin/move-ins.html (all direct PostgREST SELECT queries against public.applications and public.application_applicants).

Current Behavior: Live PostgreSQL policy app_applicants_tenant_select on application_applicants queries applications, whose permissive SELECT policies (applications_tenant_select, tenant_portal_select) query application_applicants. Every client query to applications or application_applicants fails with HTTP 500 (code: "42P17", infinite recursion detected in policy for relation "application_applicants").

Expected Behavior: Authenticated applicants should only read their own/household applications, and authenticated admins should read all applications without policy recursion.

Steps to Reproduce:

Sign in as either a tenant on /tenant/portal.html or an admin on /admin/applications.html.

Observe GET /rest/v1/applications?... fail with HTTP 500 and UI display "Could not load application details" (Tenant) or "Error loading: infinite recursion detected..." (Admin).

Severity: Critical

Recommended Correction: Break the circular reference in PostgreSQL RLS by replacing inline EXISTS (SELECT ... FROM applications ...) / EXISTS (SELECT ... FROM application_applicants ...) subqueries inside app_applicants_tenant_select, applications_tenant_select, and tenant_portal_select with SECURITY DEFINER helper functions (e.g., user_belongs_to_application(uuid)) that bypass RLS internally when resolving membership.

Issue 2 — tenant_portal_state RPC Fails (400) and Returns Incompatible Payload/Receipt Filter
Feature/Page Affected: /tenant/portal.html (tenant_portal_state PostgreSQL RPC & /js/tenant/portal.js).

Current Behavior: tenant_portal_state(p_app_id text) references v_app.lease_executed_at (a column that does not exist on public.applications), throwing SQL 42703 (HTTP 400). Furthermore, the RPC return object omits 'success': true and 'app' (expected by portal.js lines 2213–2214) and filters payment_receipts by pr.status = 'active' (an impossible value per payment_receipts_status_check, which only allows 'pending' | 'issued' | 'void').

Expected Behavior: tenant_portal_state executes cleanly, returns { success: true, app, receipts, transactions, ... }, and queries issued receipts (status = 'issued').

Steps to Reproduce:

Sign in on /tenant/portal.html with a household email.

Inspect network traffic for POST /rest/v1/rpc/tenant_portal_state -> HTTP 400.

Severity: Critical

Recommended Correction: Update tenant_portal_state to remove v_app.lease_executed_at, align its JSON response shape with portal.js (success, app, property, documents, receipts, transactions), and change the receipt status filter to pr.status IN ('issued', 'active') (or 'issued').

Issue 3 — Card Payments Silently Fail to Issue Receipts or Confirmation Emails (401 + 23503)
Feature/Page Affected: /lib/payment-router.js, /functions/api/payments/[[path]].js, /supabase/functions/confirm-card-payment/index.ts.

Current Behavior:

triggerPostPaymentConfirmation calls confirm-card-payment using the legacy service_role JWT (and Cloudflare Pages production lacks SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY in env_vars, falling back to a hardcoded legacy JWT in [[path]].js). Because Supabase Edge Function secret SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY was rotated/updated, confirm-card-payment rejects the call with 401 Unauthorized, which .catch(() => {}) swallows silently. Result: 0 receipts created and 0 payment confirmation emails sent.

Even when called with the matching Edge secret key (200 OK), confirm-card-payment/index.ts line 63 sets actorId = String(app.landlord_id || app.id || '') and passes it to issuePaymentReceipt, inserting app.id into payment_receipts.created_by. Because payment_receipts_created_by_fkey references auth.users(id), PostgreSQL throws a foreign-key violation (23503), which confirm-card-payment catches and logs as a warning, returning receipt_number: null.

Expected Behavior: Successful card payments reliably trigger confirm-card-payment, create an 'issued' receipt row + PDF in payment_receipts, and send the confirmation email.

Steps to Reproduce:

Submit an application and complete a simulated card payment (4242...) on /apply/pay.html.

Query payment_receipts and email_logs for the app_id: 0 receipt rows and 0 payment_confirmed email rows exist.

Severity: Critical

Recommended Correction:

Remove hardcoded fallback service-role keys from lib/payment-router.js and functions/api/payments/[[path]].js; configure the active SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY secret in Cloudflare Pages production env vars (and ensure confirm-card-payment either validates the active secret cleanly or checks an internal webhook secret). Do not swallow non-2xx responses in triggerPostPaymentConfirmation.

In confirm-card-payment/index.ts, pass null (or a validated auth.users.id, e.g., app.applicant_user_id if present in auth.users, otherwise null) for created_by when app.landlord_id is absent.

Issue 4 — Paid Card Applications Display "Application Fee Waived ($0.00)" on /apply/pay.html
Feature/Page Affected: /apply/js/pay.js (lines 300–322).

Current Behavior: Once a card payment succeeds (payment_status === 'paid'), /api/payments/session and /api/payments/process return amount_due_now: 0. In pay.js, session.payment_status === 'waived' || amountDueNow === 0 evaluates to true, overwriting #successHeadline with "Application Fee Waived ($0.00)" and #successSubcopy with "Your application fee is waived under an eligible credit...", even though #receiptAmountPaid shows $50.00 and Option B progress shows $100.00 / $150.00 (2/3 Paid).

Expected Behavior: Only applications with payment_status === 'waived' (or credit waiver) should show the waived headline/copy; paid card transactions must show "Payment Successful" and the card confirmation copy (or Option B remaining-members copy).

Steps to Reproduce:

Open /apply/pay.html?app_id=... for any unpaid application ($50.00 due).

Pay with test card 4242 4242 4242 4242.

Observe #successPanel displays "Application Fee Waived ($0.00)".

Severity: High

Recommended Correction: Update /apply/js/pay.js lines 300 and 305 to check session.payment_status === 'waived' || (session.payment_status !== 'paid' && amountDueNow === 0) (not amountDueNow === 0 unconditionally).

Issue 5 — Guarantors & Co-Signers Are Permanently Blocked From Confirming Screening Consent (HTTP 400)
Feature/Page Affected: /co-applicant-consent.html, confirm-co-applicant-screening Edge Function, confirm_co_applicant_screening RPC, and public.application_screening_consent_events.

Current Behavior: Live table constraint application_screening_consent_events_applicant_type_check only allows applicant_type IN ('primary', 'co_applicant'). When a Guarantor or Co-Signer submits /co-applicant-consent.html, confirm-co-applicant-screening/index.ts first saves their profile with info_completed = true (line 319), then calls confirm_co_applicant_screening RPC, which attempts INSERT INTO application_screening_consent_events with 'guarantor' / 'co_signer'. Postgres throws a check-constraint violation (23514), returning HTTP 400 ("This authorization link is invalid, expired, or already used"). Additionally, prevent_approval_without_co_applicant_consent blocks admins from approving any household with an unconsented guarantor/co-signer.

Expected Behavior: Guarantors and Co-Signers can submit Method B / Method A consent seamlessly, and their consent event is recorded under 'guarantor' or 'co_signer'.

Steps to Reproduce:

Submit an application with a Guarantor (Method A or Method B).

Open the Guarantor's /co-applicant-consent.html?token=... link, complete details, check both consent boxes, and click submit.

Observe POST /functions/v1/confirm-co-applicant-screening returns 400.

Severity: Critical

Recommended Correction: Alter application_screening_consent_events_applicant_type_check to CHECK (applicant_type = ANY (ARRAY['primary', 'co_applicant', 'guarantor', 'co_signer'])), and run the profile update + consent confirmation atomically (or roll back info_completed if RPC fails). Also confirm getSiteUrl() vs local/preview origin handling if preview environments are used.

