Issue 8 — Unauthenticated "View Receipt" Fails (401) & Cross-Origin Receipt Fetch Blocked on Non-Prod Origin
Feature/Page Affected: /apply/pay.html -> /receipt.html (/js/tenant/receipt.js & download-payment-receipt v12).

Current Behavior:

Clicking "View Receipt" from /apply/pay.html without being logged in sends no Authorization header to download-payment-receipt (which is deployed with verify_jwt: true), returning HTTP 401; fallback anon query on applications also returns 401, showing "This receipt is not available for the signed-in account. Sign in to the resident portal."

When accessing /receipt.html from a non-production origin (e.g., http://127.0.0.1:3000), download-payment-receipt returns Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://choice-properties-site.pages.dev, triggering a browser CORS failure.

Expected Behavior: Payers redirected from /apply/pay.html should either be guided seamlessly into an authenticated/tokenized receipt view (using a short-lived payment session token or signed receipt token—not an unauthenticated app_id-only PII leak) and see their receipt reliably after payment.

Steps to Reproduce:

Pay on /apply/pay.html while not signed into Supabase Auth.

Click "View Receipt". Observe 401 and error prompt.

Severity: High

Recommended Correction: Issue a scoped receipt access token (or require signed-in session / payment-session token validation inside download-payment-receipt), set verify_jwt: false on download-payment-receipt if using receipt/consent token auth (never expose full PII by app_id alone without proof), and ensure _shared/cors.ts supports configured dev/preview origins when applicable.

